{
  "_about": "Test vectors for argsDigestOf (src/record/format.js; docs/record-v1.md, Tool activity). Each vector is {name, args, canonical, digest} or {name, args, error: true}. digest is \"sha256:\" + lowercase hex SHA-256 of canonical, the RFC 8785 bytes of args. error: true means the arguments cannot be digested, and a writer omits argsDigest. JSON cannot hold every input, so args uses two tags, each an object with exactly one key: {\"$undefined\":true} is an undefined value, and {\"$number\":\"<literal>\"} is the number that literal parses to as an IEEE 754 double (e.g. \"1.0\", \"-0\", \"1e21\", \"NaN\", \"Infinity\"). Decode the tags before digesting; no vector holds a real argument of either shape.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "flat object, keys reordered",
      "args": {
        "b": 2,
        "a": 1
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}",
      "digest": "sha256:43258cff783fe7036d8a43033f830adfc60ec037382473548ac742b888292777"
    },
    {
      "name": "nested objects and arrays sort keys at every depth",
      "args": {
        "z": {
          "y": [
            {
              "d": 1,
              "c": 2
            }
          ],
          "x": null
        },
        "a": {
          "c": true,
          "b": false
        }
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":{\"b\":false,\"c\":true},\"z\":{\"x\":null,\"y\":[{\"c\":2,\"d\":1}]}}",
      "digest": "sha256:e361ba9cd9b9c2b05358b3a26828db49e7e3799a8ab9bdb2aa257247df0b2aab"
    },
    {
      "name": "keys sort by UTF-16 code units, not code points or UTF-8 bytes",
